{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Therefore you and all your assembly who are gathered.</b> That is to say: against whom you have gathered — against YHWH you have gathered. In other words, you have not made your faction against us, but against YHWH you have made it, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 2:2): ״ורוזנים נוסדו יחד״ — 'and rulers take counsel together' — and as is written (Numbers 26:9): ״בהצותם על ה׳״." "<b>And what is Aaron.</b> What has he done to you, and what is his offense against you, that you challenge his priesthood?"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Source cites תהילים ב׳:ב׳; this is Psalms 2:2. The second citation is given as במדבר כו without a verse number; resolved to Numbers 26:9 by the phrase quoted."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:02.171755787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}